{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791148495,"nonce":"yKxNA+j8WnHFhB/IVtpeK/BTRh8=","message":"Inline code alignment fixed as well.\n\nEach run was centred in its own box by half-leading, so faces with different ascent/descent splits drew on different baselines even on the same line. Measured at 15px with line-height 1.5: the UI face's baseline sits 16.92 below the box top, monospace's at 15.24. An inline code run therefore floated about 2px above the prose beside it.\n\nparagraph_div now computes each face's baseline once per line, takes the deepest, and drops each run by the difference. The code run's baseline is computed at FontWeight::Normal, since make_code_run pins it there regardless of the block's weight. The drop is rounded, because an absolute top lands on a whole pixel and letting it round implicitly left the run a pixel off.\n\nVerified by measuring the rendered ink rather than by eye. Scanning the row profile through 'into a' and through 'RichDocument' in the same frame: both now end on the same row and clear to background on the next. Before the fix the code run's ink sat three rows higher.\n\nSpacing checked the same way and is correct: a column scan across the boundary shows three background columns between 'a' and 'RichDocument', matching the 3.08px word space the measurer reports at that size. The gap before the second code run is 2px against a measured 2.35px advance.\n\nBoth numbers come from examples/rte_capture.rs, the offscreen harness, which made this iteration possible at all.","files":null}]}